      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">This enzyme is widely distributed and has been described in archaea, bacteria, yeast, plants and animals. It acts on a number of sugar alcohols, including (but not limited to) |FRAME: CPD-369 L-iditol|, |FRAME: SORBITOL D-sorbitol|, |FRAME: XYLITOL xylitol|, and |FRAME: GALACTITOL galactitol|. Enzymes from different organisms or tissues display different substrate specificity. The enzyme is specific to NAD+ and can not use NADP+.</Comment>
